{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c515","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07ad1-a1d4-7930-bd79-ab0e292ff17b"},"sequence":229,"recorded_at":1780531400000453,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4a3137a2-c6ac-464f-873d-2d1baea0e15a","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"4a3137a2-c6ac-464f-873d-2d1baea0e15a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4a3137a2-c6ac-464f-873d-2d1baea0e15a"},"call_id":"call_01a07ad2277f7ed09db8397356f55e75","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260905-3t31e9/worktree/internal/environ/shape_census_test.go`.\n1|package environ\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"go/ast\"\n5|\t\"go/parser\"\n6|\t\"go/token\"\n7|\t\"os\"\n8|\t\"path/filepath\"\n9|\t\"sort\"\n10|\t\"strconv\"\n11|\t\"strings\"\n12|\t\"testing\"\n13|)\n14|\n15|// This file is the shape layer of the shared-implementation\n16|// census. The name layer in census_test.go derives function and\n17|// method declarations by identifier and requires the derived set\n18|// to equal the ledger: it catches renames, removals, and copies\n19|// that reuse a ledgered name, but it cannot see a copy under a\n20|// fresh spelling, a new byte-counting measure, or a var-bound\n21|// alias. This layer derives implementation SHAPE from production\n22|// source and requires every shape hit to be a registered row:\n23|// a fresh spelling with the same implementation texture fails\n24|// here as an unregistered site.\n25|//\n26|// Shape space (each proven by a synthetic control in\n27|// TestShapeCensusCatchesControls, which drives the same pure\n28|// extractor the production test runs on the real tree):\n29|//\n30|//   - strict-decoder: a function that builds an encoding/json\n31|//     decoder (NewDecoder or Unmarshal) and carries a duplicate\n32|//     signal (a \"duplicate\"+\"member\" literal or a *uplicate\n33|//     identifier) in its own body or in a same-package callee.\n34|//     The callee arm covers decoders split across two local\n35|//     functions; a decoder split across packages is reuse, not\n36|//     a copy, and is not derived.\n37|//   - surrogate-gate: a function whose body holds a surrogate\n38|//     range literal (0xD800, 0xDBFF, 0xDC00, 0xDFFF in any base)\n39|//     or an identifier naming one (a *urrogate* token), or that\n40|//     references a package-level constant whose value is a\n41|//     surrogate range literal. Callers of a ledgered gate (the\n42|//     environ decoder, scalar's string decoder) trip the token\n43|//     arm and are registered as callers, not gates.\n44|//   - string-measure: a function that counts runes directly\n45|//     (a RuneCountInString/RuneCount selector).\n46|//   - byte-measure: a function with a string parameter it\n47|//     applies len() to and exactly one int result (the\n48|//     func(string)->int texture), or a function that applies\n49|//     len() to a variable assigned from a rawString() call (the\n50|//     verdict-style texture). Verdict-style measures that reuse\n51|//     a registered measure helper (stringLength and friends)\n52|//     are reuse, not copies, and are not derived.\n53|//   - var-alias: a package-level var that rebinds a ledgered\n54|//     shared-rule name, that binds a closure carrying any shape\n55|//     above, or that aliases a shape-positive local function.\n56|//     Binding an imported canonical helper under a fresh name\n57|//     (`var f = environ.StringLength`) is reuse and is clean.\n58|//\n59|// Stated residue. A decoder that never touches encoding/json (a\n60|// hand-rolled scanner with its own duplicate rule), a gate whose\n61|// bounds are derived arithmetically under fresh names with no\n62|// surrogate token anywhere, a byte measure over a non-string\n63|// parameter type, and a new grammar literal outside the four\n64|// known classes are not derived here. Each is named so the next\n65|// copy in one of those textures fails loudly by extending the\n66|// extractor, not silently.\n67|\n68|// shapeSite is one shape-derived shared-rule implementation.\n69|type shapeSite struct {\n70|\tclass  string\n71|\tpkg    string\n72|\tfile   string\n73|\tsymbol string\n74|}\n75|\n76|func (site shapeSite) key() string {\n77|\treturn site.class + \"|\" + site.pkg + \"|\" + site.file + \"|\" + site.symbol\n78|}\n79|\n80|// surrogateBounds is the UTF-16 surrogate range: any integer\n81|// literal with one of these values is a gate bound.\n82|var surrogateBounds = map[uint64]bool{\n83|\t0xD800: true,\n84|\t0xDBFF: true,\n85|\t0xDC00: true,\n86|\t0xDFFF: true,\n87|}\n88|\n89|// shapeLedger registers every shape hit in the census scope with\n90|// the rationale that keeps it honest. Canonical owners are the\n91|// single implementation new code must use; every other row names\n92|// the behavioral battery that pins it to the canonical\n93|// semantics. An unregistered hit fails the census; an orphaned\n94|// row fails it too.\n95|var shapeLedger = map[string]string{\n96|\t// Strict decoders: one JSON entry point per owner plus the\n97|\t// two envelope decoders that reach one.\n98|\t\"strict-decoder|environ|decode.go|DecodeStrictObject\":    \"canonical owner: string-walk surrogate semantics, rune measure\",\n99|\t\"strict-decoder|provhost|protocol.go|decodeStrictObject\": \"string-aware walk, pinned by frame_agreement_test.go\",\n100|\t\"strict-decoder|provhost|protocol.go|DecodeResponse\":     \"response-envelope decoder over decodeStrictObject, pinned by provhost protocol tests\",\n101|\t\"strict-decoder|provhost|status.go|DecodeStatusOutcome\":  \"status-envelope decoder over decodeStrictObject, pinned by provhost status tests\",\n102|\t\"strict-decoder|canonicaljson|canonical.go|decodeStrict\": \"canonicalizer entry over decodeValue, pinned by frame_agreement_test.go\",\n103|\t// Surrogate gates and their registered callers.\n104|\t\"surrogate-gate|environ|decode.go|HasLoneSurrogateEscape\":            \"canonical owner: string-aware walk\",\n105|\t\"surrogate-gate|environ|decode.go|DecodeStrictObject\":                \"caller: owns the gate call, pinned by frame_agreement_test.go\",\n106|\t\"surrogate-gate|provhost|surrogate.go|hasLoneSurrogateEscape\":        \"string-aware walk, pinned by frame_agreement_test.go\",\n107|\t\"surrogate-gate|provhost|protocol.go|decodeStrictObject\":             \"caller: owns the gate call, pinned by frame_agreement_test.go\",\n108|\t\"surrogate-gate|canonicaljson|canonical.go|validateSurrogateEscapes\": \"canonicalizer gate: string-aware walk, pinned by frame_agreement_test.go\",\n109|\t\"surrogate-gate|canonicaljson|canonical.go|decodeStrict\":             \"caller: owns the gate call, pinned by frame_agreement_test.go\",\n110|\t\"surrogate-gate|scalar|scalar.go|hasLoneJSONSurrogate\":               \"third spelling (raw scan, scalar-owned): unification tracked in the cross-story follow-up, behaviorally unpinned here\",\n111|\t\"surrogate-gate|scalar|scalar.go|decodeJSONString\":                   \"caller: owns the scalar gate call, pinned by the scalar suite\",\n112|\t// Rune measures: one per package plus the canonicalizer's\n113|\t// internal bounded-string helpers, which the name census\n114|\t// never saw under their fresh spellings.\n115|\t\"string-measure|environ|decode.go|StringLength\":                               \"canonical owner: runes per Section 1.6\",\n116|\t\"string-measure|provhost|opdecode.go|runeLength\":                              \"runes, pinned by measure_agreement_test.go\",\n117|\t\"string-measure|sessadapter|decode.go|stringLength\":                           \"runes, pinned by measure_agreement_test.go\",\n118|\t\"string-measure|dirnode|decode.go|stringLength\":                               \"runes, pinned by measure_agreement_test.go\",\n119|\t\"string-measure|canonicaljson|closed_shapes.go|requireBoundedString\":          \"canonicalizer-internal rune bound, pinned by the canonicaljson suite\",\n120|\t\"string-measure|canonicaljson|closed_shapes.go|validateBlobDescriptor\":        \"canonicalizer-internal rune bound, pinned by the canonicaljson suite\",\n121|\t\"string-measure|canonicaljson|closed_shapes.go|validateManifestEntries\":       \"canonicalizer-internal rune bound, pinned by the canonicaljson suite\",\n122|\t\"string-measure|canonicaljson|core_records.go|nullableBoundedString\":          \"canonicalizer-internal rune bound, pinned by the canonicaljson suite\",\n123|\t\"string-measure|canonicaljson|core_records.go|validateProviderIdentityRecord\": \"canonicalizer-internal rune bound, pinned by identity_agreement_test.go opaque rows\",\n124|\t\"string-measure|scalar|path.go|ParseAbsolutePath\":                             \"grammar-owner path bound, pinned by the scalar suite\",\n125|\t// Byte measures: the two Section 5.1 exec gates.\n126|\t\"byte-measure|provhost|spawn.go|checkSpawnArgv\":        \"bytes by specification, pinned by TestByteBoundsStayBytes\",\n127|\t\"byte-measure|provhost|spawn.go|checkSpawnEnvLiterals\": \"bytes by specification, pinned by TestByteBoundsStayBytes\",\n128|}\n129|\n130|// packageShapes is the per-package extractor state: which local\n131|// functions carry a duplicate signal or a shape, and which\n132|// package-level constants hold surrogate bounds.\n133|type packageShapes struct {\n134|\tfuncDups   map[string]bool\n135|\tfuncShapes map[string][]string\n136|\tconstBound map[string]bool\n137|}\n138|\n139|// TestSharedShapesAreLedgered requires every shape-derived site\n140|// to be a registered row, and every row to be derived: an\n141|// unregistered copy fails as a unification violation, and a row\n142|// naming an implementation production no longer derives fails\n143|// as orphaned.\n144|func TestSharedShapesAreLedgered(t *testing.T) {\n145|\tderived := deriveShapeSites(t)\n146|\tfor key := range derived {\n147|\t\tif _, ok := shapeLedger[key]; !ok {\n148|\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"unregistered shared-rule copy %q: add one canonical implementation in internal/environ instead, or register the shape with its agreement battery\", key)\n149|\t\t}\n150|\t}\n151|\tfor key, rationale := range shapeLedger {\n152|\t\tif !derived[key] {\n153|\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"orphaned shape row %q (%s): production no longer derives it\", key, rationale)\n154|\t\t}\n155|\t}\n156|}\n157|\n158|// deriveShapeSites walks the census scope and derives every\n159|// shape site from production source.\n160|func deriveShapeSites(t *testing.T) map[string]bool {\n161|\tt.Helper()\n162|\troot, err := internalRoot(t)\n163|\tif err != nil {\n164|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"shapes: %v\", err)\n165|\t}\n166|\tsources := readScopeSources(t, root)\n167|\tsites := map[string]bool{}\n168|\tfor pkg, files := range sources {\n169|\t\tfor _, site := range shapeSitesInPackage(pkg, files) {\n170|\t\t\tsites[site.key()] = true\n171|\t\t}\n172|\t}\n173|\tif len(sites) == 0 {\n174|\t\tt.Fatal(\"shapes derived zero sites; the scanner is blind, not the tree clean\")\n175|\t}\n176|\treturn sites\n177|}\n178|\n179|// readScopeSources reads every production Go file in the census\n180|// packages into memory, keyed by package then file name.\n181|func readScopeSources(t *testing.T, root string) map[string]map[string][]byte {\n182|\tt.Helper()\n183|\tsources := map[string]map[string][]byte{}\n184|\tcount := 0\n185|\terr := filepath.Walk(root, func(path string, info os.FileInfo, err error) error {\n186|\t\tif err != nil {\n187|\t\t\treturn err\n188|\t\t}\n189|\t\tif info.IsDir() || !strings.HasSuffix(path, \".go\") || strings.HasSuffix(path, \"_test.go\") {\n190|\t\t\treturn nil\n191|\t\t}\n192|\t\trel, err := filepath.Rel(root, path)\n193|\t\tif err != nil {\n194|\t\t\treturn err\n195|\t\t}\n196|\t\tparts := strings.Split(rel, string(filepath.Separator))\n197|\t\tpkg := parts[0]\n198|\t\tif !censusPackages[pkg] {\n199|\t\t\treturn nil\n200|\t\t}\n201|\t\tsource, err := os.ReadFile(path)\n202|\t\tif err != nil {\n203|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"shapes: read %s: %v\", path, err)\n204|\t\t}\n205|\t\tif sources[pkg] == nil {\n206|\t\t\tsources[pkg] = map[string][]byte{}\n207|\t\t}\n208|\t\tsources[pkg][parts[len(parts)-1]] = source\n209|\t\tcount++\n210|\t\treturn nil\n211|\t})\n212|\tif err != nil {\n213|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"shapes: walk: %v\", err)\n214|\t}\n215|\tif count == 0 {\n216|\t\tt.Fatal(\"shapes scanned zero files; the scanner is broken, not the tree\")\n217|\t}\n218|\treturn sources\n219|}\n220|\n221|// shapeSitesInPackage derives the shape sites of one package. It\n222|// is pure over its inputs, so the synthetic controls drive this\n223|// exact function on planted sources: a control that fails here\n224|// fails the production census by construction.\n225|func shapeSitesInPackage(pkg string, files map[string][]byte) []shapeSite {\n226|\tparsed := map[string]*ast.File{}\n227|\tfor file, source := range files {\n228|\t\tsyntax, err := parser.ParseFile(token.NewFileSet(), file, source, 0)\n229|\t\tif err != nil {\n230|\t\t\treturn []shapeSite{{class: \"parse-failure\", pkg: pkg, file: file, symbol: \"unparseable\"}}\n231|\t\t}\n232|\t\tparsed[file] = syntax\n233|\t}\n234|\tstate := &packageShapes{funcDups: map[string]bool{}, funcShapes: map[string][]string{}, constBound: map[string]bool{}}\n235|\tfor _, syntax := range parsed {\n236|\t\tfor _, decl := range syntax.Decls {\n237|\t\t\tswitch node := decl.(type) {\n238|\t\t\tcase *ast.FuncDecl:\n239|\t\t\t\tif node.Body == nil {\n240|\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n241|\t\t\t\t}\n242|\t\t\t\tif bodyHasDupSignal(node.Body) {\n243|\t\t\t\t\tstate.funcDups[node.Name.Name] = true\n244|\t\t\t\t}\n245|\t\t\tcase *ast.GenDecl:\n246|\t\t\t\tfor _, spec := range node.Specs {\n247|\t\t\t\t\tvalue, ok := spec.(*ast.ValueSpec)\n248|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n249|\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n250|\t\t\t\t\t}\n251|\t\t\t\t\tfor index, name := range value.Names {\n252|\t\t\t\t\t\tif index >= len(value.Values) {\n253|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n254|\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n255|\t\t\t\t\t\tif literal, ok := value.Values[index].(*ast.BasicLit); ok && literal.Kind == token.INT {\n256|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tif magnitude, err := strconv.ParseUint(literal.Value, 0, 32); err == nil && surrogateBounds[magnitude] {\n257|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tstate.constBound[name.Name] = true\n258|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n259|\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n260|\t\t\t\t\t}\n261|\t\t\t\t}\n262|\t\t\t}\n263|\t\t}\n264|\t}\n265|\tfor _, syntax := range parsed {\n266|\t\tfor _, decl := range syntax.Decls {\n267|\t\t\tnode, ok := decl.(*ast.FuncDecl)\n268|\t\t\tif !ok || node.Body == nil {\n269|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n270|\t\t\t}\n271|\t\t\t// Same-named methods union their shapes so the\n272|\t\t\t// alias resolution below is file-order\n273|\t\t\t// independent.\n274|\t\t\tunion := map[string]bool{}\n275|\t\t\tfor _, class := range state.funcShapes[node.Name.Name] {\n276|\t\t\t\tunion[class] = true\n277|\t\t\t}\n278|\t\t\tfor _, class := range funcShapeClasses(node.Body, node.Type, state) {\n279|\t\t\t\tunion[class] = true\n280|\t\t\t}\n281|\t\t\tvar merged []string\n282|\t\t\tfor class := range union {\n283|\t\t\t\tmerged = append(merged, class)\n284|\t\t\t}\n285|\t\t\tsort.Strings(merged)\n286|\t\t\tstate.funcShapes[node.Name.Name] = merged\n287|\t\t}\n288|\t}\n289|\tvar sites []shapeSite\n290|\tadd := func(class, file, symbol string) {\n291|\t\tsites = append(sites, shapeSite{class: class, pkg: pkg, file: file, symbol: symbol})\n292|\t}\n293|\tfor file, syntax := range parsed {\n294|\t\tfor _, decl := range syntax.Decls {\n295|\t\t\tswitch node := decl.(type) {\n296|\t\t\tcase *ast.FuncDecl:\n297|\t\t\t\tif node.Body == nil {\n298|\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n299|\t\t\t\t}\n300|\t\t\t\t// Emission uses the file-local shapes; the\n301|\t\t\t\t// union map above serves alias resolution\n302|\t\t\t\t// only, so same-named methods never bleed\n303|\t\t\t\t// sites across files.\n304|\t\t\t\tfor _, class := range funcShapeClasses(node.Body, node.Type, state) {\n305|\t\t\t\t\tadd(class, file, node.Name.Name)\n306|\t\t\t\t}\n307|\t\t\t\tast.Inspect(node.Body, func(inner ast.Node) bool {\n308|\t\t\t\t\tliteral, ok := inner.(*ast.FuncLit)\n309|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n310|\t\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n311|\t\t\t\t\t}\n312|\t\t\t\t\tfor _, class := range funcShapeClasses(literal.Body, literal.Type, state) {\n313|\t\t\t\t\t\tadd(class, file, node.Name.Name+\"$closure\")\n314|\t\t\t\t\t}\n315|\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n316|\t\t\t\t})\n317|\t\t\tcase *ast.GenDecl:\n318|\t\t\t\tfor _, spec := range node.Specs {\n319|\t\t\t\t\tvalue, ok := spec.(*ast.ValueSpec)\n320|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n321|\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n322|\t\t\t\t\t}\n323|\t\t\t\t\tfor _, name := range value.Names {\n324|\t\t\t\t\t\tif class, ok := sharedFunctionSymbols[name.Name]; ok {\n325|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tadd(class, file, name.Name)\n326|\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n327|\t\t\t\t\t\tfor _, rhs := range value.Values {\n328|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tswitch bound := rhs.(type) {\n329|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tcase *ast.FuncLit:\n330|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tfor _, class := range funcShapeClasses(bound.Body, bound.Type, state) {\n331|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tadd(class, file, name.Name)\n332|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n333|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tcase *ast.Ident:\n334|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t// `var f = localHelper` rebinds a\n335|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t// local implementation: it inherits\n336|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t// the helper's shapes. Binding an\n337|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t// imported helper (`var f =\n338|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t// otherpkg.Helper`) is a selector,\n339|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t// not an identifier, and is reuse.\n340|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tfor _, class := range state.funcShapes[bound.Name] {\n341|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tadd(class, file, name.Name)\n342|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n343|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n344|\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n345|\t\t\t\t\t}\n346|\t\t\t\t}\n347|\t\t\t}\n348|\t\t}\n349|\t}\n350|\treturn sites\n351|}\n352|\n353|// funcShapeClasses reports the shape classes of one function or\n354|// closure body.\n355|func funcShapeClasses(body *ast.BlockStmt, sig *ast.FuncType, state *packageShapes) []string {\n356|\tif body == nil {\n357|\t\treturn nil\n358|\t}\n359|\tseen := map[string]bool{}\n360|\tif bodyBuildsJSONDecoder(body) && bodyCarriesDupSignal(body, state) {\n361|\t\tseen[\"strict-decoder\"] = true\n362|\t}\n363|\tif bodyCarriesSurrogateSignal(body, state) {\n364|\t\tseen[\"surrogate-gate\"] = true\n365|\t}\n366|\tif bodyCountsRunes(body) {\n367|\t\tseen[\"string-measure\"] = true\n368|\t}\n369|\tif bodyIsByteMeasure(body, sig) {\n370|\t\tseen[\"byte-measure\"] = true\n371|\t}\n372|\tif _, ok := bodyIsVerdictByteMeasure(body); ok {\n373|\t\tseen[\"byte-measure\"] = true\n374|\t}\n375|\tvar classes []string\n376|\tfor class := range seen {\n377|\t\tclasses = append(classes, class)\n378|\t}\n379|\tsort.Strings(classes)\n380|\treturn classes\n381|}\n382|\n383|// bodyBuildsJSONDecoder reports whether the body constructs an\n384|// encoding/json decoder or unmarshaler.\n385|func bodyBuildsJSONDecoder(body *ast.BlockStmt) bool {\n386|\tfound := false\n387|\tast.Inspect(body, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n388|\t\tcall, ok := node.(*ast.CallExpr)\n389|\t\tif !ok {\n390|\t\t\treturn true\n391|\t\t}\n392|\t\tselector, ok := call.Fun.(*ast.SelectorExpr)\n393|\t\tif !ok {\n394|\t\t\treturn true\n395|\t\t}\n396|\t\tidentifier, ok := selector.X.(*ast.Ident)\n397|\t\tif !ok || identifier.Name != \"json\" {\n398|\t\t\treturn true\n399|\t\t}\n400|\t\tif selector.Sel.Name == \"NewDecoder\" || selector.Sel.Name == \"Unmarshal\" {\n401|\t\t\tfound = true\n402|\t\t\treturn false\n403|\t\t}\n404|\t\treturn true\n405|\t})\n406|\treturn found\n407|}\n408|\n409|// bodyHasDupSignal reports whether the body carries a duplicate\n410|// signal: a literal naming both halves, or an identifier with\n411|// the duplicate root (a FaultDuplicate-style constant, a\n412|// duplicate map probe, a dup-check helper name).\n413|func bodyHasDupSignal(body *ast.BlockStmt) bool {\n414|\tfound := false\n415|\tast.Inspect(body, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n416|\t\tswitch n := node.(type) {\n417|\t\tcase *ast.BasicLit:\n418|\t\t\tif n.Kind == token.STRING {\n419|\t\t\t\tif text, err := strconv.Unquote(n.Value); err == nil {\n420|\t\t\t\t\tif strings.Contains(text, \"duplicate\") && strings.Contains(text, \"member\") {\n421|\t\t\t\t\t\tfound = true\n422|\t\t\t\t\t\treturn false\n423|\t\t\t\t\t}\n424|\t\t\t\t}\n425|\t\t\t}\n426|\t\tcase *ast.Ident:\n427|\t\t\tif strings.Contains(n.Name, \"uplicate\") {\n428|\t\t\t\tfound = true\n429|\t\t\t\treturn false\n430|\t\t\t}\n431|\t\t}\n432|\t\treturn true\n433|\t})\n434|\treturn found\n435|}\n436|\n437|// bodyCarriesDupSignal extends the own-body signal across\n438|// same-package callees: a decoder split into an entry plus a\n439|// local duplicate helper still derives on the entry.\n440|func bodyCarriesDupSignal(body *ast.BlockStmt, state *packageShapes) bool {\n441|\tif bodyHasDupSignal(body) {\n442|\t\treturn true\n443|\t}\n444|\tcallee := false\n445|\tast.Inspect(body, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n446|\t\tcall, ok := node.(*ast.CallExpr)\n447|\t\tif !ok {\n448|\t\t\treturn true\n449|\t\t}\n450|\t\tswitch fun := call.Fun.(type) {\n451|\t\tcase *ast.Ident:\n452|\t\t\tif state.funcDups[fun.Name] {\n453|\t\t\t\tcallee = true\n454|\t\t\t\treturn false\n455|\t\t\t}\n456|\t\tcase *ast.SelectorExpr:\n457|\t\t\tif state.funcDups[fun.Sel.Name] {\n458|\t\t\t\tcallee = true\n459|\t\t\t\treturn false\n460|\t\t\t}\n461|\t\t}\n462|\t\treturn true\n463|\t})\n464|\treturn callee\n465|}\n466|\n467|// bodyCarriesSurrogateSignal reports whether the body holds a\n468|// surrogate range literal, names one, or references a\n469|// package-level bound constant.\n470|func bodyCarriesSurrogateSignal(body *ast.BlockStmt, state *packageShapes) bool {\n471|\tfound := false\n472|\tast.Inspect(body, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n473|\t\tswitch n := node.(type) {\n474|\t\tcase *ast.BasicLit:\n475|\t\t\tif n.Kind == token.INT {\n476|\t\t\t\tif magnitude, err := strconv.ParseUint(n.Value, 0, 32); err == nil && surrogateBounds[magnitude] {\n477|\t\t\t\t\tfound = true\n478|\t\t\t\t\treturn false\n479|\t\t\t\t}\n480|\t\t\t}\n481|\t\tcase *ast.Ident:\n482|\t\t\tif strings.Contains(strings.ToLower(n.Name), \"urrogate\") {\n483|\t\t\t\tfound = true\n484|\t\t\t\treturn false\n485|\t\t\t}\n486|\t\t\tif state.constBound[n.Name] {\n487|\t\t\t\tfound = true\n488|\t\t\t\treturn false\n489|\t\t\t}\n490|\t\t}\n491|\t\treturn true\n492|\t})\n493|\treturn found\n494|}\n495|\n496|// bodyCountsRunes reports whether the body counts runes\n497|// directly through the utf8 selector.\n498|func bodyCountsRunes(body *ast.BlockStmt) bool {\n499|\tfound := false\n500|\tast.Inspect(body, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c517","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07ad1-a1d4-7930-bd79-ab0e292ff17b"},"sequence":230,"recorded_at":1780531400000455,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4a3137a2-c6ac-464f-873d-2d1baea0e15a","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"4a3137a2-c6ac-464f-873d-2d1baea0e15a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4a3137a2-c6ac-464f-873d-2d1baea0e15a"},"call_id":"call_01a07ad228227db3a152c1617085a6cb","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260905-3t31e9/worktree/internal/environ/frame_agreement_test.go`.\n1|package environ_test\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"go/ast\"\n5|\t\"go/parser\"\n6|\t\"go/token\"\n7|\t\"os\"\n8|\t\"path/filepath\"\n9|\t\"strconv\"\n10|\t\"strings\"\n11|\t\"testing\"\n12|\n13|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/canonicaljson\"\n14|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/dirnode\"\n15|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/environ\"\n16|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/provhost\"\n17|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/sessadapter\"\n18|)\n19|\n20|// This file is the cross-facade frame-agreement battery. Every\n21|// Section 7.8, 7.9, and provider-protocol body crosses a strict\n22|// object decoder before any member is trusted, and each facade\n23|// carries its own copy of that decoder (ledgered in\n24|// census_test.go). The battery drives one shared corpus through\n25|// all five judges — environ.DecodeStrictObject,\n26|// sessadapter.DecodeTuple, dirnode.CheckScanRequest,\n27|// provhost.DecodeManifest, and canonicaljson.Canonicalize — and\n28|// requires the ledgered verdict at each.\n29|//\n30|// A row whose reached arm cannot be determined fails, never\n31|// passes: frame-fault rows assert the full rendering (the fault\n32|// detail phrase in the refusal text), and accept rows assert the\n33|// body travels past the frame gate (an accept, or a refusal at a\n34|// named later arm with the frame phrase asserted absent). A code\n35|//-only assertion would conflate the frame gate with the member\n36|// gates behind it, which carry the same refusal code.\n37|//\n38|// The roster fails closed in both directions: every fault detail\n39|// derived from environ production must own at least one row, and\n40|// a row naming a detail production no longer derives fails as\n41|// orphaned. Expected verdicts are ledgered per judge, so a\n42|// verdict flip in EITHER direction — a fix or a regression —\n43|// reddens its row instead of passing silently.\n44|\n45|// frameRow is one corpus vector with the ledgered verdict at\n46|// every judge. A refuse expectation names the refusal text the\n47|// verdict must contain; an accept expectation names a later-arm\n48|// text the verdict must contain (\"\" with accept=true means the\n49|// entry itself accepts). canonicalRefuse nil means the\n50|// canonicalizer is not judged on this row: it validates JSON\n51|// values, not closed objects, so object-shape faults\n52|// (non-object, duplicate, trailing) are outside the decoder\n53|// rules it shares with the facades.\n54|type frameRow struct {\n55|\tfault string\n56|\tname  string\n57|\tbody  []byte\n58|\n59|\t// Per-judge bodies override body where an entry needs a\n60|\t// shaped vector (accept controls): nil means the shared\n61|\t// minimal body, which every frame gate refuses before any\n62|\t// member is read.\n63|\tsessBody []byte\n64|\tdirBody  []byte\n65|\tprovBody []byte\n66|\n67|\tenvironRefuse string\n68|\tenvironMember string\n69|\n70|\tsessAccept bool\n71|\tsessText   string\n72|\tsessAbsent string\n73|\n74|\tdirAccept bool\n75|\tdirText   string\n76|\tdirAbsent string\n77|\n78|\tprovAccept bool\n79|\tprovText   string\n80|\tprovAbsent string\n81|\n82|\tcanonicalRefuse *bool\n83|}\n84|\n85|func boolPointer(value bool) *bool {\n86|\treturn &value\n87|}\n88|\n89|// frameCorpus is the shared fault corpus. Surrogate subclasses\n90|// enumerate the full shape of the gate: bare highs and lows,\n91|// mispairs, truncated and malformed escapes, paired controls,\n92|// backslash-run parity (runs of 1..3 backslashes before the\n93|// escape, in value, member-name, and nested positions), and the\n94|// composed shapes an even run plus a FOLLOWING real escape. Run\n95|// parity plus composition proves both directions of the old\n96|// raw-scan divergence instead of one: a `\\u` sequence behind an\n97|// odd run is a real escape every judge refuses when lone, while\n98|// the same sequence behind an even run is quoted text the frame\n99|// gate admits (the member arms behind it still refuse the\n100|// minimal bodies, with the frame phrase asserted absent). The\n101|// composed rows close the sampling hole the first battery left:\n102|// an even run followed by a real lone escape is refused by the\n103|// string walk, while the raw scan misread the quoted text as a\n104|// high surrogate, paired it with the following real escape, and\n105|// admitted a body encoding/json silently rewrote to U+FFFD.\n106|func frameCorpus() []frameRow {\n107|\tpairVersion := `\"environment_version\":\"A\\uD83D\\uDE00B\"`\n108|\tpairTuple := []byte(strings.Replace(validTupleJSON(), `\"environment_version\":\"2.1.0\"`, pairVersion, 1))\n109|\tpairCursor := validScanRequestJSON(`\"A\\uD83D\\uDE00B\"`)\n110|\trows := []frameRow{\n111|\t\t{\n112|\t\t\tfault: environ.FaultNotUTF8, name: \"non-utf8 bytes\",\n113|\t\t\tbody:          []byte(\"{\\\"v\\\":\\\"a\\xff\\\"}\"),\n114|\t\t\tenvironRefuse: environ.FaultNotUTF8,\n115|\t\t\tsessText:      environ.FaultNotUTF8, dirText: environ.FaultNotUTF8, provText: environ.FaultNotUTF8,\n116|\t\t\tcanonicalRefuse: boolPointer(true),\n117|\t\t},\n118|\t\t{\n119|\t\t\tfault: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate, name: \"bare high escape\",\n120|\t\t\tbody:          []byte(\"{\\\"v\\\":\\\"A\\\\ud800B\\\"}\"),\n121|\t\t\tenvironRefuse: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate,\n122|\t\t\tsessText:      environ.FaultLoneSurrogate, dirText: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate, provText: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate,\n123|\t\t\tcanonicalRefuse: boolPointer(true),\n124|\t\t},\n125|\t\t{\n126|\t\t\tfault: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate, name: \"bare low escape\",\n127|\t\t\tbody:          []byte(\"{\\\"v\\\":\\\"A\\\\udc00B\\\"}\"),\n128|\t\t\tenvironRefuse: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate,\n129|\t\t\tsessText:      environ.FaultLoneSurrogate, dirText: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate, provText: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate,\n130|\t\t\tcanonicalRefuse: boolPointer(true),\n131|\t\t},\n132|\t\t{\n133|\t\t\tfault: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate, name: \"high followed by non-low\",\n134|\t\t\tbody:          []byte(\"{\\\"v\\\":\\\"A\\\\uD83D\\\\u0041B\\\"}\"),\n135|\t\t\tenvironRefuse: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate,\n136|\t\t\tsessText:      environ.FaultLoneSurrogate, dirText: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate, provText: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate,\n137|\t\t\tcanonicalRefuse: boolPointer(true),\n138|\t\t},\n139|\t\t{\n140|\t\t\t// Truncated and malformed escapes are not well-formed\n141|\t\t\t// \\uXXXX escapes, so the surrogate gate passes them\n142|\t\t\t// to the syntax arms on every judge.\n143|\t\t\tfault: environ.FaultNotObject, name: \"truncated escape falls to syntax\",\n144|\t\t\tbody:          []byte(\"{\\\"v\\\":\\\"A\\\\uD83\\\"}\"),\n145|\t\t\tenvironRefuse: environ.FaultNotObject, environMember: \"v\",\n146|\t\t\tsessText: \"environment tuple not a JSON object\", sessAbsent: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate,\n147|\t\t\tdirText: \"scan request not a JSON object\", dirAbsent: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate,\n148|\t\t\tprovText:        environ.FaultNotObject,\n149|\t\t\tcanonicalRefuse: boolPointer(true),\n150|\t\t},\n151|\t\t{\n152|\t\t\tfault: environ.FaultNotObject, name: \"malformed escape falls to syntax\",\n153|\t\t\tbody:          []byte(\"{\\\"v\\\":\\\"A\\\\uDEFG B\\\"}\"),\n154|\t\t\tenvironRefuse: environ.FaultNotObject, environMember: \"v\",\n155|\t\t\tsessText: \"environment tuple not a JSON object\", sessAbsent: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate,\n156|\t\t\tdirText: \"scan request not a JSON object\", dirAbsent: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate,\n157|\t\t\tprovText:        environ.FaultNotObject,\n158|\t\t\tcanonicalRefuse: boolPointer(true),\n159|\t\t},\n160|\t\t{\n161|\t\t\t// An even backslash run quotes the following text:\n162|\t\t\t// the frame gate admits and the member arms refuse,\n163|\t\t\t// with the frame phrase asserted absent. Before the\n164|\t\t\t// facade delegation the raw scan refused these at\n165|\t\t\t// the surrogate arm; the flip is the recorded fix.\n166|\t\t\tfault: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate, name: \"escaped backslash high run2\",\n167|\t\t\tbody:     []byte(\"{\\\"v\\\":\\\"A\\\\\\\\ud800B\\\"}\"),\n168|\t\t\tsessText: \"environment tuple carries unknown member\", sessAbsent: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate,\n169|\t\t\tdirText: \"scan request carries unknown member\", dirAbsent: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate,\n170|\t\t\tprovText: \"manifest carries unknown member\", provAbsent: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate,\n171|\t\t\tcanonicalRefuse: boolPointer(false),\n172|\t\t},\n173|\t\t{\n174|\t\t\t// Run 3 is an escaped backslash followed by a REAL\n175|\t\t\t// lone escape (value `A\\` plus U+D800), so every\n176|\t\t\t// judge refuses: odd runs escape, even runs quote.\n177|\t\t\tfault: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate, name: \"escaped backslash high run3\",\n178|\t\t\tbody:          []byte(\"{\\\"v\\\":\\\"A\\\\\\\\\\\\ud800B\\\"}\"),\n179|\t\t\tenvironRefuse: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate,\n180|\t\t\tsessText:      environ.FaultLoneSurrogate, dirText: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate, provText: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate,\n181|\t\t\tcanonicalRefuse: boolPointer(true),\n182|\t\t},\n183|\t\t{\n184|\t\t\tfault: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate, name: \"escaped backslash low run2\",\n185|\t\t\tbody:     []byte(\"{\\\"v\\\":\\\"A\\\\\\\\udc00B\\\"}\"),\n186|\t\t\tsessText: \"environment tuple carries unknown member\", sessAbsent: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate,\n187|\t\t\tdirText: \"scan request carries unknown member\", dirAbsent: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate,\n188|\t\t\tprovText: \"manifest carries unknown member\", provAbsent: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate,\n189|\t\t\tcanonicalRefuse: boolPointer(false),\n190|\t\t},\n191|\t\t{\n192|\t\t\tfault: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate, name: \"escaped backslash pair run2\",\n193|\t\t\tbody:     []byte(\"{\\\"v\\\":\\\"A\\\\\\\\uD83D\\\\\\\\uDE00B\\\"}\"),\n194|\t\t\tsessText: \"environment tuple carries unknown member\", sessAbsent: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate,\n195|\t\t\tdirText: \"scan request carries unknown member\", dirAbsent: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate,\n196|\t\t\tprovText: \"manifest carries unknown member\", provAbsent: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate,\n197|\t\t\tcanonicalRefuse: boolPointer(false),\n198|\t\t},\n199|\t\t{\n200|\t\t\tfault: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate, name: \"escaped backslash in member name\",\n201|\t\t\tbody:     []byte(\"{\\\"A\\\\\\\\ud800B\\\":1}\"),\n202|\t\t\tsessText: \"environment tuple carries unknown member\", sessAbsent: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate,\n203|\t\t\tdirText: \"scan request carries unknown member\", dirAbsent: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate,\n204|\t\t\tprovText: \"manifest carries unknown member\", provAbsent: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate,\n205|\t\t\tcanonicalRefuse: boolPointer(false),\n206|\t\t},\n207|\t\t{\n208|\t\t\tfault: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate, name: \"escaped backslash nested\",\n209|\t\t\tbody:     []byte(\"{\\\"v\\\":{\\\"w\\\":\\\"A\\\\\\\\ud800B\\\"}}\"),\n210|\t\t\tsessText: \"environment tuple carries unknown member\", sessAbsent: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate,\n211|\t\t\tdirText: \"scan request carries unknown member\", dirAbsent: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate,\n212|\t\t\tprovText: \"manifest carries unknown member\", provAbsent: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate,\n213|\t\t\tcanonicalRefuse: boolPointer(false),\n214|\t\t},\n215|\t\t{\n216|\t\t\t// An even run followed by a REAL lone low escape:\n217|\t\t\t// the string walk consumes the `\\\\` pair, reads\n218|\t\t\t// quoted text, then refuses the real lone escape.\n219|\t\t\t// The raw scan misread the quoted text as a high\n220|\t\t\t// surrogate, paired it with the real low escape,\n221|\t\t\t// and admitted the body. This row is the composed\n222|\t\t\t// shape the first battery never sampled.\n223|\t\t\tfault: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate, name: \"escaped backslash plus real lone low\",\n224|\t\t\tbody:          []byte(\"{\\\"v\\\":\\\"A\\\\\\\\ud800\\\\udc00B\\\"}\"),\n225|\t\t\tenvironRefuse: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate,\n226|\t\t\tsessText:      environ.FaultLoneSurrogate, dirText: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate, provText: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate,\n227|\t\t\tcanonicalRefuse: boolPointer(true),\n228|\t\t},\n229|\t\t{\n230|\t\t\t// The same composition with a real lone high\n231|\t\t\t// escape behind the even run: every judge refuses.\n232|\t\t\tfault: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate, name: \"escaped backslash plus real lone high\",\n233|\t\t\tbody:          []byte(\"{\\\"v\\\":\\\"A\\\\\\\\udc00\\\\ud800B\\\"}\"),\n234|\t\t\tenvironRefuse: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate,\n235|\t\t\tsessText:      environ.FaultLoneSurrogate, dirText: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate, provText: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate,\n236|\t\t\tcanonicalRefuse: boolPointer(true),\n237|\t\t},\n238|\t\t{\n239|\t\t\t// An even run followed by a REAL pair: the frame\n240|\t\t\t// gate admits on every judge and the member arms\n241|\t\t\t// refuse, with the frame phrase asserted absent.\n242|\t\t\t// Before the facade delegation the raw scan\n243|\t\t\t// refused this at the surrogate arm (it misread\n244|\t\t\t// the quoted text as a high surrogate followed by\n245|\t\t\t// a non-low), so this row proves the composed\n246|\t\t\t// shape on the over-strict side too.\n247|\t\t\tfault: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate, name: \"escaped backslash plus real pair\",\n248|\t\t\tbody:     []byte(\"{\\\"v\\\":\\\"A\\\\\\\\ud800\\\\uD83D\\\\uDE00B\\\"}\"),\n249|\t\t\tsessText: \"environment tuple carries unknown member\", sessAbsent: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate,\n250|\t\t\tdirText: \"scan request carries unknown member\", dirAbsent: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate,\n251|\t\t\tprovText: \"manifest carries unknown member\", provAbsent: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate,\n252|\t\t\tcanonicalRefuse: boolPointer(false),\n253|\t\t},\n254|\t\t{\n255|\t\t\tfault: environ.FaultDuplicate, name: \"duplicate member\",\n256|\t\t\tbody:          []byte(\"{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"v\\\":2}\"),\n257|\t\t\tenvironRefuse: environ.FaultDuplicate, environMember: \"v\",\n258|\t\t\tsessText: environ.FaultDuplicate, dirText: environ.FaultDuplicate, provText: environ.FaultDuplicate,\n259|\t\t},\n260|\t\t{\n261|\t\t\tfault: environ.FaultTrailing, name: \"trailing data\",\n262|\t\t\tbody:          []byte(\"{\\\"v\\\":1} {}\"),\n263|\t\t\tenvironRefuse: environ.FaultTrailing,\n264|\t\t\tsessText:      environ.FaultTrailing, dirText: environ.FaultTrailing, provText: environ.FaultTrailing,\n265|\t\t},\n266|\t\t{\n267|\t\t\tfault: environ.FaultNotObject, name: \"non-object top level\",\n268|\t\t\tbody:          []byte(\"[1,2]\"),\n269|\t\t\tenvironRefuse: environ.FaultNotObject,\n270|\t\t\tsessText:      environ.FaultNotObject, dirText: environ.FaultNotObject, provText: environ.FaultNotObject,\n271|\t\t},\n272|\t\t{\n273|\t\t\tfault: environ.FaultNotObject, name: \"unterminated string is syntax\",\n274|\t\t\tbody:          []byte(\"{\\\"v\\\":\\\"abc\"),\n275|\t\t\tenvironRefuse: environ.FaultNotObject, environMember: \"v\",\n276|\t\t\tsessText: environ.FaultNotObject, dirText: environ.FaultNotObject, provText: environ.FaultNotObject,\n277|\t\t\tcanonicalRefuse: boolPointer(true),\n278|\t\t},\n279|\t\t{\n280|\t\t\tfault: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate, name: \"paired surrogates admit\",\n281|\t\t\tbody:       []byte(`{\"v\":\"A\\uD83D\\uDE00B\"}`),\n282|\t\t\tsessBody:   pairTuple,\n283|\t\t\tdirBody:    pairCursor,\n284|\t\t\tprovBody:   []byte(`{\"note\":\"A\\uD83D\\uDE00B\"}`),\n285|\t\t\tsessAccept: true,\n286|\t\t\tdirAccept:  true,\n287|\t\t\tprovText:   \"manifest carries unknown member\", provAbsent: environ.FaultLoneSurrogate,\n288|\t\t\tcanonicalRefuse: boolPointer(false),\n289|\t\t},\n290|\t\t{\n291|\t\t\tfault: environ.FaultNotUTF8, name: \"multibyte text admits\",\n292|\t\t\tbody:       []byte(\"{\\\"v\\\":\\\"plain ü ☃\\\"}\"),\n293|\t\t\tsessBody:   pairTuple,\n294|\t\t\tdirBody:    pairCursor,\n295|\t\t\tprovBody:   []byte(\"{\\\"note\\\":\\\"plain ü ☃\\\"}\"),\n296|\t\t\tsessAccept: true,\n297|\t\t\tdirAccept:  true,\n298|\t\t\tprovText:   \"manifest carries unknown member\", provAbsent: environ.FaultNotUTF8,\n299|\t\t\tcanonicalRefuse: boolPointer(false),\n300|\t\t},\n301|\t}\n302|\treturn rows\n303|}\n304|\n305|// deriveFaultDetails derives the frame-fault space from environ\n306|// production: every Fault* constant value in decode.go. A sixth\n307|// fault shape fails the roster below instead of passing\n308|// unrostered.\n309|func deriveFaultDetails(t *testing.T) map[string]bool {\n310|\tt.Helper()\n311|\tpath := filepath.Join(mustGetwd(t), \"decode.go\")\n312|\tsource, err := os.ReadFile(path)\n313|\tif err != nil {\n314|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"faults: %v\", err)\n315|\t}\n316|\tsyntax, err := parser.ParseFile(token.NewFileSet(), path, source, 0)\n317|\tif err != nil {\n318|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"faults: %v\", err)\n319|\t}\n320|\tdetails := map[string]bool{}\n321|\tfor _, decl := range syntax.Decls {\n322|\t\tnode, ok := decl.(*ast.GenDecl)\n323|\t\tif !ok {\n324|\t\t\tcontinue\n325|\t\t}\n326|\t\tfor _, spec := range node.Specs {\n327|\t\t\tvalue, ok := spec.(*ast.ValueSpec)\n328|\t\t\tif !ok {\n329|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n330|\t\t\t}\n331|\t\t\tfor index, name := range value.Names {\n332|\t\t\t\tif !strings.HasPrefix(name.Name, \"Fault\") || index >= len(value.Values) {\n333|\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n334|\t\t\t\t}\n335|\t\t\t\tliteral, ok := value.Values[index].(*ast.BasicLit)\n336|\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n337|\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"faults: %s is not a literal; the extractor cannot see through indirection\", name.Name)\n338|\t\t\t\t}\n339|\t\t\t\ttext, err := strconv.Unquote(literal.Value)\n340|\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n341|\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"faults: %v\", err)\n342|\t\t\t\t}\n343|\t\t\t\tdetails[text] = true\n344|\t\t\t}\n345|\t\t}\n346|\t}\n347|\tif len(details) == 0 {\n348|\t\tt.Fatal(\"faults derived zero details; the scanner is blind, not the space empty\")\n349|\t}\n350|\treturn details\n351|}\n352|\n353|func mustGetwd(t *testing.T) string {\n354|\tt.Helper()\n355|\tdirectory, err := os.Getwd()\n356|\tif err != nil {\n357|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"frame: %v\", err)\n358|\t}\n359|\treturn directory\n360|}\n361|\n362|// TestFrameFaultRosterIsClosed requires every derived fault\n363|// detail to own at least one row, and every row to name a\n364|// derived detail.\n365|func TestFrameFaultRosterIsClosed(t *testing.T) {\n366|\tdetails := deriveFaultDetails(t)\n367|\tcovered := map[string]bool{}\n368|\tfor _, row := range frameCorpus() {\n369|\t\tif row.fault == \"\" {\n370|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"row %q names no fault detail\", row.name)\n371|\t\t}\n372|\t\tif !details[row.fault] {\n373|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"row %q names underived detail %q\", row.name, row.fault)\n374|\t\t}\n375|\t\tcovered[row.fault] = true\n376|\t}\n377|\tfor detail := range details {\n378|\t\tif !covered[detail] {\n379|\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"derived fault detail %q owns no corpus row\", detail)\n380|\t\t}\n381|\t}\n382|}\n383|\n384|// TestFrameAgreementAcrossFacades drives the shared corpus\n385|// through all five judges and requires the ledgered verdict at\n386|// each. environ rows assert the exact fault and member; facade\n387|// rows assert the full frame rendering (the detail phrase in the\n388|// refusal text) or, for accept rows, travel past the frame gate\n389|// with the frame phrase asserted absent; canonical rows assert\n390|// the verdict only, where the canonicalizer shares the rule.\n391|func TestFrameAgreementAcrossFacades(t *testing.T) {\n392|\tfor _, row := range frameCorpus() {\n393|\t\tt.Run(row.name, func(t *testing.T) {\n394|\t\t\t_, fault := environ.DecodeStrictObject(row.body)\n395|\t\t\tif row.environRefuse == \"\" {\n396|\t\t\t\tif fault != nil {\n397|\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"environ refused %q: %v\", row.body, fault)\n398|\t\t\t\t}\n399|\t\t\t} else {\n400|\t\t\t\tif fault == nil {\n401|\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"environ admitted %q, want fault %q\", row.body, row.environRefuse)\n402|\t\t\t\t}\n403|\t\t\t\tif fault.Detail != row.environRefuse || fault.Member != row.environMember {\n404|\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"environ fault = (%q, %q), want (%q, %q)\", fault.Detail, fault.Member, row.environRefuse, row.environMember)\n405|\t\t\t\t}\n406|\t\t\t}\n407|\t\t\tsessBody := orBody(row.body, row.sessBody)\n408|\t\t\tdirBody := orBody(row.body, row.dirBody)\n409|\t\t\tprovBody := orBody(row.body, row.provBody)\n410|\t\t\tassertFacadeVerdict(t, \"sessadapter\", sessBody, row.sessAccept, row.sessText, row.sessAbsent, func(body []byte) error {\n411|\t\t\t\t_, err := sessadapter.DecodeTuple(body)\n412|\t\t\t\treturn err\n413|\t\t\t})\n414|\t\t\tassertFacadeVerdict(t, \"dirnode\", dirBody, row.dirAccept, row.dirText, row.dirAbsent, func(body []byte) error {\n415|\t\t\t\t_, err := dirnode.CheckScanRequest(body)\n416|\t\t\t\treturn err\n417|\t\t\t})\n418|\t\t\tassertFacadeVerdict(t, \"provhost\", provBody, row.provAccept, row.provText, row.provAbsent, func(body []byte) error {\n419|\t\t\t\treturn provhost.DecodeManifest(body)\n420|\t\t\t})\n421|\t\t\tif row.canonicalRefuse != nil {\n422|\t\t\t\t_, err := canonicaljson.Canonicalize(row.body)\n423|\t\t\t\tif (*row.canonicalRefuse && err == nil) || (!*row.canonicalRefuse && err != nil) {\n424|\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"canonicaljson verdict = refuse=%v, want refuse=%v (err=%v)\", err != nil, *row.canonicalRefuse, err)\n425|\t\t\t\t}\n426|\t\t\t}\n427|\t\t})\n428|\t}\n429|}\n430|\n431|// orBody selects the per-judge override body when present.\n432|func orBody(shared, override []byte) []byte {\n433|\tif override != nil {\n434|\t\treturn override\n435|\t}\n436|\treturn shared\n437|}\n438|\n439|// assertFacadeVerdict requires the ledgered verdict at one\n440|// facade entry: an accept, or a refusal whose text contains the\n441|// frame phrase (and never contains the absent phrase, which\n442|// pins travel past a gate the body must cross).\n443|func assertFacadeVerdict(t *testing.T, facade string, body []byte, accept bool, text, absent string, drive func([]byte) error) {\n444|\tt.Helper()\n445|\terr := drive(body)\n446|\tif accept {\n447|\t\tif err != nil {\n448|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s refused %q, want accept: %v\", facade, body, err)\n449|\t\t}\n450|\t\treturn\n451|\t}\n452|\tif err == nil {\n453|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s admitted %q, want refusal containing %q\", facade, body, text)\n454|\t}\n455|\tif text != \"\" && !strings.Contains(err.Error(), text) {\n456|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s error = %v, want text containing %q\", facade, err, text)\n457|\t}\n458|\tif absent != \"\" && strings.Contains(err.Error(), absent) {\n459|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s error = %v, must not contain %q\", facade, err, absent)\n460|\t}\n461|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c519","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07ad1-a1d4-7930-bd79-ab0e292ff17b"},"sequence":231,"recorded_at":1780531400000457,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4a3137a2-c6ac-464f-873d-2d1baea0e15a","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"4a3137a2-c6ac-464f-873d-2d1baea0e15a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4a3137a2-c6ac-464f-873d-2d1baea0e15a"},"call_id":"call_01a07ad228d977818691284d1766bd3b","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260905-3t31e9/worktree/internal/environ/measure_agreement_test.go`.\n1|package environ_test\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"fmt\"\n5|\t\"strings\"\n6|\t\"testing\"\n7|\n8|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/canonicaljson\"\n9|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/dirnode\"\n10|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/environ\"\n11|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/provhost\"\n12|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n13|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/sessadapter\"\n14|)\n15|\n16|// This file is the cross-facade string-measure battery. Section\n17|// 1.6 bounds strings in characters, not bytes: string[1..128]\n18|// admits 128 characters of any width. Two strict decoders both\n19|// blind to lone surrogates was one drift class the cross-story\n20|// review found; byte-vs-rune bounds disagreeing on a member that\n21|// crosses both protocols was another. This battery pins the\n22|// measure at every character-bound member one facade shares with\n23|// another, with multibyte vectors that separate the measures: a\n24|// 128-`é` value is 128 characters but 256 bytes, so a\n25|// byte-measure refuses what the specification admits.\n26|//\n27|// The byte side is ledgered, not left open. Provider SpawnPlan\n28|// argv elements and totals and env-literal values bound BYTES by\n29|// Section 5.1 (outside this story), implemented in exactly two\n30|// functions — provhost checkSpawnArgv and checkSpawnEnvLiterals\n31|// — and the byte rows below drive all three byte gates through\n32|// the production DecodeSpawnPlan entry. validEnvName measures\n33|// len() over an ASCII-only grammar where bytes and runes\n34|// coincide, so no row can separate them; that is stated here,\n35|// not hidden. Every other string bound in the census scope flows\n36|// through the single measure helper of its package (census\n37|// ledger: StringLength, runeLength, stringLength), and the rune\n38|// rows pin the helper verdicts at one crossing member per\n39|// facade plus every provhost rune site.\n40|\n41|// validSpawnJSON is one valid Provider SpawnPlan body with the\n42|// given profile mapping, first extra argv element, literal value,\n43|// and native session ID literal. The argv always carries one\n44|// short flag so element-count rules hold while one member under\n45|// test varies.\n46|func validSpawnJSON(mapping, extraArgv, literalValue, nativeID string) []byte {\n47|\targv := `[\"--serve\"]`\n48|\tif extraArgv != \"\" {\n49|\t\targv = fmt.Sprintf(`[\"--serve\",%s]`, jsonQuote(extraArgv))\n50|\t}\n51|\tliterals := `{}`\n52|\tif literalValue != \"\" {\n53|\t\tliterals = fmt.Sprintf(`{\"EXTRA_KEY\":%s}`, jsonQuote(literalValue))\n54|\t}\n55|\tnative := `null`\n56|\tif nativeID != \"\" {\n57|\t\tnative = jsonQuote(nativeID)\n58|\t}\n59|\treturn []byte(fmt.Sprintf(`{\"argv\":%s,\"cwd\":\"/tmp/ax\",\"env_names\":[],\"env_literals\":%s,\"native_session_id\":%s,\"profile_mapping\":%s,\"extensions\":{}}`,\n60|\t\targv, literals, native, jsonQuote(mapping)))\n61|}\n62|\n63|// validSpawnMapping returns the production YOLO flag for codex:\n64|// scaffolding for rows whose probe point is a different member,\n65|// so a mapping change cannot break them for the wrong reason.\n66|// Rows whose probe point IS the mapping construct their own\n67|// lengths and never call this.\n68|func validSpawnMapping(t *testing.T) string {\n69|\tt.Helper()\n70|\tmapping, err := provhost.ProfileMapping(\"codex\", provhost.ProfileYOLO)\n71|\tif err != nil {\n72|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"scaffolding: %v\", err)\n73|\t}\n74|\treturn mapping\n75|}\n76|\n77|// jsonQuote quotes a Go string as a JSON string literal.\n78|func jsonQuote(value string) string {\n79|\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%q\", value)\n80|}\n81|\n82|// TestStringMeasureCountsRunes proves the character measure at\n83|// the unit helper and at one crossing member per facade. Each\n84|// accept vector carries more bytes than its bound, so a\n85|// byte-measure would refuse it; each refuse vector carries one\n86|// character too many, so a widened bound would admit it.\n87|func TestStringMeasureCountsRunes(t *testing.T) {\n88|\tascii128 := strings.Repeat(\"v\", 128)\n89|\twide128 := strings.Repeat(\"é\", 128)\n90|\twide129 := strings.Repeat(\"é\", 129)\n91|\twide512 := strings.Repeat(\"é\", 512)\n92|\twide513 := strings.Repeat(\"é\", 513)\n93|\twide1024 := strings.Repeat(\"é\", 1024)\n94|\twide1025 := strings.Repeat(\"é\", 1025)\n95|\twide4096 := strings.Repeat(\"é\", 4096)\n96|\twide4097 := strings.Repeat(\"é\", 4097)\n97|\tt.Run(\"environ helper\", func(t *testing.T) {\n98|\t\tif _, ok := environ.CheckStringBounds([]byte(jsonQuote(wide128)), 1, 128); !ok {\n99|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"environ.CheckStringBounds refused 128 characters in 256 bytes\")\n100|\t\t}\n101|\t\tif _, ok := environ.CheckStringBounds([]byte(jsonQuote(wide129)), 1, 128); ok {\n102|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"environ.CheckStringBounds admitted 129 characters\")\n103|\t\t}\n104|\t\tif _, ok := environ.CheckStringBounds([]byte(jsonQuote(ascii128)), 1, 128); !ok {\n105|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"environ.CheckStringBounds refused 128 ASCII characters\")\n106|\t\t}\n107|\t})\n108|\tt.Run(\"sessadapter tuple version\", func(t *testing.T) {\n109|\t\taccept := []byte(strings.Replace(validTupleJSON(), `\"2.1.0\"`, jsonQuote(wide128), 1))\n110|\t\tif _, err := sessadapter.DecodeTuple(accept); err != nil {\n111|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"DecodeTuple refused 128-character version: %v\", err)\n112|\t\t}\n113|\t\trefuse := []byte(strings.Replace(validTupleJSON(), `\"2.1.0\"`, jsonQuote(wide129), 1))\n114|\t\t_, err := sessadapter.DecodeTuple(refuse)\n115|\t\tif err == nil {\n116|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"DecodeTuple admitted 129-character version\")\n117|\t\t}\n118|\t\tif !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"string[1..128]\") {\n119|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"DecodeTuple error = %v, want the version bound arm\", err)\n120|\t\t}\n121|\t})\n122|\tt.Run(\"dirnode scan cursor\", func(t *testing.T) {\n123|\t\tif _, err := dirnode.CheckScanRequest(validScanRequestJSON(jsonQuote(wide4096))); err != nil {\n124|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"CheckScanRequest refused 4096-character cursor: %v\", err)\n125|\t\t}\n126|\t\t_, err := dirnode.CheckScanRequest(validScanRequestJSON(jsonQuote(wide4097)))\n127|\t\tif err == nil {\n128|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"CheckScanRequest admitted 4097-character cursor\")\n129|\t\t}\n130|\t\tif !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"string[1..4096]\") {\n131|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"CheckScanRequest error = %v, want the cursor bound arm\", err)\n132|\t\t}\n133|\t})\n134|\tt.Run(\"provhost profile mapping bound arm\", func(t *testing.T) {\n135|\t\tbound := validSpawnJSON(strings.Repeat(\"m\", 513), \"\", \"\", \"\")\n136|\t\terr := provhost.DecodeSpawnPlan(bound, \"codex\", provhost.ProfileYOLO, scalar.PlatformLinux)\n137|\t\tif err == nil {\n138|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"DecodeSpawnPlan admitted 513-character mapping\")\n139|\t\t}\n140|\t\tif !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"not at most 512 characters\") {\n141|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"DecodeSpawnPlan error = %v, want the mapping bound arm\", err)\n142|\t\t}\n143|\t})\n144|\tt.Run(\"provhost mapping admits 300 wide characters\", func(t *testing.T) {\n145|\t\t// 300 `é` is 300 characters but 600 bytes: the bound\n146|\t\t// arm must admit it (runes) and the equality arm must\n147|\t\t// refuse it (it is not the provider mapping). A byte\n148|\t\t// measure would fire the bound arm instead.\n149|\t\twide := validSpawnJSON(strings.Repeat(\"é\", 300), \"\", \"\", \"\")\n150|\t\terr := provhost.DecodeSpawnPlan(wide, \"codex\", provhost.ProfileYOLO, scalar.PlatformLinux)\n151|\t\tif err == nil {\n152|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"DecodeSpawnPlan admitted a mapping that is not the provider mapping\")\n153|\t\t}\n154|\t\tif !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"does not match the provider profile\") {\n155|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"DecodeSpawnPlan error = %v, want the mapping equality arm, not the bound arm\", err)\n156|\t\t}\n157|\t})\n158|\tt.Run(\"provhost native session id bound\", func(t *testing.T) {\n159|\t\tmapping := validSpawnMapping(t)\n160|\t\taccept := validSpawnJSON(mapping, \"\", \"\", wide512)\n161|\t\tif err := provhost.DecodeSpawnPlan(accept, \"codex\", provhost.ProfileYOLO, scalar.PlatformLinux); err != nil {\n162|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"DecodeSpawnPlan refused 512-character native session id: %v\", err)\n163|\t\t}\n164|\t\trefuse := validSpawnJSON(mapping, \"\", \"\", wide513)\n165|\t\terr := provhost.DecodeSpawnPlan(refuse, \"codex\", provhost.ProfileYOLO, scalar.PlatformLinux)\n166|\t\tif err == nil {\n167|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"DecodeSpawnPlan admitted 513-character native session id\")\n168|\t\t}\n169|\t\tif !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"1..512 characters\") {\n170|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"DecodeSpawnPlan error = %v, want the native session id bound arm\", err)\n171|\t\t}\n172|\t})\n173|\tt.Run(\"identity opaque bound agrees\", func(t *testing.T) {\n174|\t\t// The opaque_identity value bound (1..1024 runes) is\n175|\t\t// the one member validated by both identity dialects:\n176|\t\t// both judges must agree on the multibyte edges.\n177|\t\taccept := mutateMember(t, validIdentityJSON(), \"opaque_identity\", `{\"k\":`+jsonQuote(wide1024)+`}`)\n178|\t\tif err := provhost.CheckIdentity(accept, \"antigravity\"); err != nil {\n179|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"CheckIdentity refused 1024-character opaque value: %v\", err)\n180|\t\t}\n181|\t\tif _, _, err := canonicaljson.CalculateObjectIdentity(accept); err != nil {\n182|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"CalculateObjectIdentity refused 1024-character opaque value: %v\", err)\n183|\t\t}\n184|\t\trefuse := mutateMember(t, validIdentityJSON(), \"opaque_identity\", `{\"k\":`+jsonQuote(wide1025)+`}`)\n185|\t\tif err := provhost.CheckIdentity(refuse, \"antigravity\"); err == nil {\n186|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"CheckIdentity admitted 1025-character opaque value\")\n187|\t\t}\n188|\t\tif _, _, err := canonicaljson.CalculateObjectIdentity(refuse); err == nil {\n189|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"CalculateObjectIdentity admitted 1025-character opaque value\")\n190|\t\t}\n191|\t})\n192|}\n193|\n194|// TestByteBoundsStayBytes proves the three ledgered byte gates\n195|// keep measuring bytes: each vector is within the rune bound a\n196|// character measure would enforce but over the byte bound the\n197|// specification states, so a rune-measure regression would admit\n198|// it and travel to a later arm instead of the byte arm.\n199|func TestByteBoundsStayBytes(t *testing.T) {\n200|\tmapping := validSpawnMapping(t)\n201|\tt.Run(\"argv element bytes\", func(t *testing.T) {\n202|\t\t// 2049 `é` is 2049 characters but 4098 bytes.\n203|\t\tbody := validSpawnJSON(mapping, strings.Repeat(\"é\", 2049), \"\", \"\")\n204|\t\terr := provhost.DecodeSpawnPlan(body, \"codex\", provhost.ProfileYOLO, scalar.PlatformLinux)\n205|\t\tif err == nil {\n206|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"DecodeSpawnPlan admitted a 4098-byte argv element\")\n207|\t\t}\n208|\t\tif !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"NUL-free bytes\") {\n209|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"DecodeSpawnPlan error = %v, want the argv element byte arm\", err)\n210|\t\t}\n211|\t})\n212|\tt.Run(\"argv total bytes\", func(t *testing.T) {\n213|\t\t// Seventeen 4000-byte elements pass the element gate\n214|\t\t// and fail the 65536-byte total.\n215|\t\telements := make([]string, 0, 17)\n216|\t\tfor index := 0; index < 17; index++ {\n217|\t\t\telements = append(elements, jsonQuote(strings.Repeat(\"a\", 4000)))\n218|\t\t}\n219|\t\tbody := []byte(fmt.Sprintf(`{\"argv\":[\"--serve\",%s],\"cwd\":\"/tmp/ax\",\"env_names\":[],\"env_literals\":{},\"native_session_id\":null,\"profile_mapping\":%s,\"extensions\":{}}`,\n220|\t\t\tstrings.Join(elements, \",\"), jsonQuote(mapping)))\n221|\t\terr := provhost.DecodeSpawnPlan(body, \"codex\", provhost.ProfileYOLO, scalar.PlatformLinux)\n222|\t\tif err == nil {\n223|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"DecodeSpawnPlan admitted argv over 65536 total bytes\")\n224|\t\t}\n225|\t\tif !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"65536 bytes total\") {\n226|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"DecodeSpawnPlan error = %v, want the argv total byte arm\", err)\n227|\t\t}\n228|\t})\n229|\tt.Run(\"env literal bytes\", func(t *testing.T) {\n230|\t\tbody := validSpawnJSON(mapping, \"\", strings.Repeat(\"é\", 2049), \"\")\n231|\t\terr := provhost.DecodeSpawnPlan(body, \"codex\", provhost.ProfileYOLO, scalar.PlatformLinux)\n232|\t\tif err == nil {\n233|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"DecodeSpawnPlan admitted a 4098-byte env literal\")\n234|\t\t}\n235|\t\tif !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"4096 NUL-free bytes\") {\n236|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"DecodeSpawnPlan error = %v, want the env literal byte arm\", err)\n237|\t\t}\n238|\t})\n239|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
