{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c551","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07ad1-a1d4-7930-bd79-ab0e292ff17b"},"sequence":259,"recorded_at":1780531400000513,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4a3137a2-c6ac-464f-873d-2d1baea0e15a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"4a3137a2-c6ac-464f-873d-2d1baea0e15a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4a3137a2-c6ac-464f-873d-2d1baea0e15a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"824b80e7-26c4-41c0-9775-7396cee13466"},"task_id":"824b80e7-26c4-41c0-9775-7396cee13466","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"824b80e7-26c4-41c0-9775-7396cee13466","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260905-3t31e9/worktree/internal/provhost/surrogate.go`.\n1|package provhost\n2|\n3|// This file is the local lone-surrogate gate for the Section 1.6 wire\n4|// bodies this package decodes. Pinned specification Section 1.6 requires\n5|// decoders to reject lone surrogate code points before canonicalization,\n6|// and the repository already enforces that rule in\n7|// internal/canonicaljson (validateSurrogateEscapes, called from\n8|// decodeStrict). This package decodes with its own strict object reader\n9|// (decodeStrictObject in protocol.go) because it must keep member-level\n10|// fault attribution (duplicate member names, the offending member) that\n11|// the shared decoder does not report, and encoding/json silently replaces\n12|// a lone \\ud800-style escape with U+FFFD instead of failing. So the gate\n13|// lives here, scans the raw frame bytes before decoding, and refuses the\n14|// same class the shared package refuses.\n15|//\n16|// The gate is deliberately a copy, not an import: internal/canonicaljson\n17|// is byte-identical shared baseline text that two unlanded stories must\n18|// not edit at once, so neither story may add an export there. The\n19|// surrogate-vector sweep in surrogate_test.go drives both this gate\n20|// (through decodeStrictObject) and canonicaljson.Canonicalize over a\n21|// derived enumeration of the code-point space, so the copies cannot\n22|// drift silently: a divergence reddens there rather than passing\n23|// unnoticed. The sweep judges verdicts against the independent\n24|// implementation, never against a shared hand-written expectation.\n25|//\n26|// The gate decides the surrogate-escape question only. Malformed\n27|// escapes and unterminated strings are not its verdict: they fall\n28|// through to the JSON-syntax arms that already own them. Non-UTF-8\n29|// bytes never reach it: decodeStrictObject refuses them first,\n30|// because a raw WTF-8 surrogate encoding would otherwise slip past\n31|// this escape scanner and be silently replaced with U+FFFD by\n32|// encoding/json. A lone high surrogate is a high unit not immediately\n33|// followed by a \\uDC00–\\uDFFF escape; a lone low surrogate is a low\n34|// unit in any other position. Both are refused before any member is\n35|// read.\n36|\n37|// The gate's own range constants: the high and low surrogate halves\n38|// of the Section 1.6 verdict space. The\n39|// surrogate-vector sweep in surrogate_test.go derives its pair-second\n40|// dimension from these constants arithmetically (bounds plus and minus\n41|// small offsets), so the boundary neighborhood is enumerated from the\n42|// gate rather than from a hand-written literal: shifting a bound here\n43|// moves the swept neighborhood with it instead of silently uncovering\n44|// it. Verdicts still come from the independent implementation, never\n45|// from these constants, so a wrong bound reddens against the oracle.\n46|const (\n47|\thighSurrogateMin = 0xd800\n48|\thighSurrogateMax = 0xdbff\n49|\tlowSurrogateMin  = 0xdc00\n50|\tlowSurrogateMax  = 0xdfff\n51|)\n52|\n53|// hasLoneSurrogateEscape reports whether raw JSON bytes carry a lone\n54|// surrogate escape inside any string. The string walk mirrors the shared\n55|// package's walker (backslash handling included: a \\\\ escape consumes\n56|// both bytes, so the text \"\\\\ud800\" is backslash-plus-text, not an\n57|// escape), but only the surrogate verdict is returned.\n58|func hasLoneSurrogateEscape(input []byte) bool {\n59|\tfor index := 0; index < len(input); index++ {\n60|\t\tif input[index] != '\"' {\n61|\t\t\tcontinue\n62|\t\t}\n63|\t\tfor index++; index < len(input); index++ {\n64|\t\t\tif input[index] == '\"' {\n65|\t\t\t\tgoto stringComplete\n66|\t\t\t}\n67|\t\t\tif input[index] != '\\\\' {\n68|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n69|\t\t\t}\n70|\t\t\tindex++\n71|\t\t\tif index >= len(input) || input[index] != 'u' {\n72|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n73|\t\t\t}\n74|\t\t\tunit, end, ok := readHexUnit(input, index-1)\n75|\t\t\tif !ok {\n76|\t\t\t\t// Not a well-formed \\uXXXX escape: the\n77|\t\t\t\t// JSON-syntax arms own it, not this gate.\n78|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n79|\t\t\t}\n80|\t\t\tindex = end - 1\n81|\t\t\tif unit >= highSurrogateMin && unit <= highSurrogateMax {\n82|\t\t\t\tlow, lowEnd, ok := readHexUnit(input, end)\n83|\t\t\t\tif !ok || low < lowSurrogateMin || low > lowSurrogateMax {\n84|\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n85|\t\t\t\t}\n86|\t\t\t\tindex = lowEnd - 1\n87|\t\t\t} else if unit >= lowSurrogateMin && unit <= lowSurrogateMax {\n88|\t\t\t\treturn true\n89|\t\t\t}\n90|\t\t}\n91|\t\t// The string never closed: malformed JSON the syntax arms\n92|\t\t// refuse, so the gate claims no surrogate verdict here.\n93|\t\treturn false\n94|\tstringComplete:\n95|\t}\n96|\treturn false\n97|}\n98|\n99|// readHexUnit parses one \\uXXXX escape at input[start]. It reports false\n100|// when the bytes are not a well-formed escape; hex digits parse in\n101|// either case, matching the shared package's ParseUint base-16 read.\n102|func readHexUnit(input []byte, start int) (uint16, int, bool) {\n103|\tif start < 0 || start+6 > len(input) || input[start] != '\\\\' || input[start+1] != 'u' {\n104|\t\treturn 0, start, false\n105|\t}\n106|\tvar value uint16\n107|\tfor _, b := range input[start+2 : start+6] {\n108|\t\tvar digit byte\n109|\t\tif b >= '0' && b <= '9' {\n110|\t\t\tdigit = b - '0'\n111|\t\t} else if b >= 'a' && b <= 'f' {\n112|\t\t\tdigit = b - 'a' + 10\n113|\t\t} else if b >= 'A' && b <= 'F' {\n114|\t\t\tdigit = b - 'A' + 10\n115|\t\t} else {\n116|\t\t\treturn 0, start, false\n117|\t\t}\n118|\t\tvalue = value*16 + uint16(digit)\n119|\t}\n120|\treturn value, start + 6, true\n121|}"}}}
