ethod `(*Registry).Reconcile` absorbed by the bare-name dedupe; P3 dead multi-line BackendID arm missed by the line-text filter. Post-fix both RED in one `TestBackendIDEntryCensus` run: `has no census pair` for the multiline site, `collide on one bare name: Reconcile: Reconcile in manifest.go against Registry.Reconcile in manifest.go`. Plants reverted byte-identical (`git diff` shows no PLANT; full suite green).\\n- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-2okwyf_outcome-r4.md` + `TASK-260906-2okwyf_battery-r4.json` + `TASK-260906-2okwyf_mutants-r4.json` (r4: 5 applied — narrowing 2, arm-deletion 2, census-only 1 — 4 killed / 1 survived with a plant-evidenced bound; NOT_APPLIED/COMPILE_FAIL distinct controls; masks non-empty: census 15, behav 32). Continuity re-runs on this tree: r1 9/9, r2 5/5, r3 6/6 killed, 0 survived — cumulative 24/25 with the single survivor D-tb-entryindex-enforce (0 live collisions; P2 plant GREEN without the gate, RED with it). N3 deliberately left open with the 0-of-44 sweep bound. Candidate tree OID in the outcome doc, detached-index write-tree AFTER this append, `ls-tree` read back against the scope enumeration both directions.\\n- GATES: `go test ./...` exit 0 (23 ok, 0 FAIL), `-race` terminalbackend exit 0, `-cover` exit 0 (tb 95.4%, ph 86.0%, pv 97.8%), `go vet ./...` exit 0, `GOOS=windows go vet` (tb/ph/pv) exit 0, `go build` + `GOOS=windows go build` exit 0, gofmt clean.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps).\\n\\n### 1015 — 2okwyf round 3: F2 instrument — Reconcile entry gate plus (site, entry) census, 41/41\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260906-2okwyf rework (review rev2 CHANGES REQUESTED, blocking F2: site-keyed census read 31/31 while Reconcile echoed at manifest.go:1726/:1762; control plant C1 left the whole suite green). Production: `manifest.go` only — `Reconcile` validates both `manifest.TerminalBackendID` and `probe.TerminalBackendID` through `ParseID` before any check runs (manifest.go:1696/1699; same pattern as CheckVersionTuple/CheckProviderDescriptor). Test: new `internal/terminalbackend/backend_id_entry_census_test.go` (~1300 lines) — derived census keyed by (site, reaching exported entry): 41 pairs + 1 site exemption + 1 pair exemption; every pair carries a guard statement, a hostile-noecho battery through its entry (2 hostile shapes), and a validated fire (12 own fires with recorder attribution + 29 inventoried-witness citations resolved mechanically against DeclaredArmIdentities); entry coverage over all derived exported entries (59 derived: 10 pair entries + 5 hostile-only batteried + 44 free with reasons). `ParseID` comment rewritten to state what the instrument enforces, nothing beyond.\\n- FINDING (F2 confirmed pre-fix): hostile structs through production `Reconcile` rendered 305B (`executable substitution`) and 313B (`probe generation binding`) refusals containing the whole string. Red-before: new census `reconcile` battery FAILs (both shapes, both arms); post-fix 41/41 PASS. C1 (ParseID guard out of CheckProviderDescriptor) fails closed on exactly the new test (308B echo) while the rest of the package suite stays green — reproducing the reviewer's plant and proving the instrument, not the old suite, holds the class.\\n- FINDING (shadowed pair): CheckProviderDescriptor's digest-parse arm is unreachable via AdmitProviderDescriptor (ParseProviderDescriptor's own digest arm fires first) — carried as an executed exempt pair with a shadow pin, not a 42nd pair. Registration.validate's digest-null arm stays the single site exemption (white-box pin executed in-file).\\n- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-2okwyf_outcome-r3.md` + `TASK-260906-2okwyf_battery-r3.json` + `TASK-260906-2okwyf_mutants-r3.json` (6 applied/6 killed/0 survived: narrowing 1 N-tb-reconcile-lengthgated with len27-fail/len221-pass split, arm-deletion 2 D-tb-reconcile-entry + D-tb-checkdesc-entry(C1), ordering 1 R-tb-checktuple-order [N2: correctly refiled from narrowing], census-only 1 C-tb-reconcile-deadarm, audit-only 1 S-tb-statusresult-shadow killed only by the full-run audit naming conformance.go:765; NOT_APPLIED/COMPILE_FAIL distinct control rows; masks non-empty; bodies in JSON). N1: anchors re-derived on the final tree (Reconcile guards manifest.go:1696/1699, sites :1741/:1777/:2099/:2102; descriptor guard terminalbackend.go:646; ParseID census note :163). Candidate tree OID in the outcome doc, computed AFTER the LOGBOOK append, verified by `ls-tree`.\\n- GATES: `go test ./...` exit 0 (23 ok, 0 FAIL), `-race` terminalbackend exit 0, `-cover` exit 0 (tb 95.4%, ph 86.0%, pv 97.8%), `go vet ./...` exit 0, `go build` + `GOOS=windows go build` exit 0, gofmt clean.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 5895,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1474,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
