Uint53 (guarded) but hardened identically everywhere.\n+- FINDING (union coverage): in-package + external test files compile to one binary, so the TestMain audit sees exercised sites from both; the in-package driver table is load-bearing for the two frame-fault passthrough sites (external corpora carry no frame-faulty tuple/observation bodies). Proven: dropping one passthrough driver fails the closed rule set (`want exactly 39 codes, observed 38`).\n+- FINDING (mutant quality): M13n v1 (presence skip without decode skip) survived — the nil member refuses at decode fall-through. v2 (with `continue`) kills. R_rawstringerr predicted-survivor was wrong: direct-rawString arms (platform/arch/version/provider) refuse at the wrong arm, killed by exact-text drivers.\n+- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-33xcnc_outcome.md` + battery log + mutants JSON + harness + mutant table (54 killed/55 applied on denominator 90 = 31 refuse + 59 bool; 34 narrowing incl. T1/C3 token-preserving raw-scans; 3 census-only; 1 audit-only; 1 predicted survivor R_digestnonstr with downstream-hold bound; H1/H2 prove NOT_APPLIED/COMPILE_FAIL rows). Callerless closed for 10 Check* symbols via delegation; DecodeTuple/DecodeEnvironmentObservation/rawUint53/Fault.Error/HasLoneSurrogateEscape re-stated with reasons.\n+- GATES: `go test ./...` exit 0 (23 ok), `-race` exit 0 (environ/sessadapter/dirnode/scalar/provhost/canonicaljson/provider; full-repo race not run), `-cover` exit 0 (env 92.4/sess 82.0/dir 87.7/ph 86.0/scalar 90.1), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet` + both builds exit 0, gofmt clean, tracecheck exit 0, catalog current, cigate selections exit 0, fuzz smoke 13/13.\n+- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review. Open need (in outcome, no board element): provhost decoder convergence needs unfreezing `provhost/protocol.go`.\n+\n+### 1111 — 2okwyf round 4: F3 stray file out of the tree, N1/N2 instrument gates fail closed, N3/N4 bounds\n"}}}
